## 9. API Security and Access Control

The RaceDay API applies role-based access control to ensure that users can only perform operations appropriate to their responsibilities. Public endpoints allow users to register, authenticate and view publicly available event information. Participants are provided with functionality relating to their enrolments, while organisers are given additional permissions to create and manage events, categories, results, routes and weather information.

This approach improves the security and integrity of the system by preventing unauthorised users from performing administrative operations. Authentication is required for protected resources, while the user's assigned role determines which operations can be performed.

## 10. Conclusion

The API Endpoint Plan provides a structured specification for communication between the RaceDay application and its backend services. The endpoints correspond with the entities and functionality identified in the system design and database structure. The use of RESTful HTTP methods, defined request bodies, expected responses and role-based access provides a clear foundation for implementing the RaceDay Web API.
